# GNU Stow ignore list (stow >= 2.4).
#
# This repo is stowed from its root into $HOME:
#
#   cd ~/mydotfiles && stow --dotfiles -t "$HOME" .
#
# Patterns are Perl regexes matched against each path relative to the package
# root. Keep them unanchored to `^/` — stow strips the leading slash before
# matching, so `^/bin` never fires while `^bin` does.
#
# What stow manages here: `.config/<tool>` directories only (directory-level
# links, so caches such as nvim's `lazy/` stay inside the repo).
#
# NOT stowed, on purpose:
#   bin/    install.sh links these into ~/.local/bin (stow cannot rename)
#   shell/  install.sh links zshrc/zshenv/zshrc_custom to renamed $HOME files
#   tests/  repo-only harness
#   Code/   VS Code rewrites its own tree; install.sh owns those three files

# --- repo metadata -----------------------------------------------------------
^\.git$
^\.gitignore$
^\.stow-local-ignore$
^README\.md$
^AGENTS\.md$
^CLAUDE\.md$
^skills-lock\.json$

# --- deploys elsewhere / repo-only ------------------------------------------
^install\.sh$
^bin$
^shell$
^tests$
^docs$

# --- generated tutorials ----------------------------------------------------
\.html$

# --- owned by install.sh (VS Code rewrites these at runtime) ----------------
^\.config/Code$
